# The Retrosheet source files. ~2.1 GB unpacked, fetched by update_data.py,
# and identical for everyone — there is nothing to be gained by versioning it.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose. Unanchored, "data/" matches a
# directory of that name at any depth, which silently swallows docs/data —
# the entire exported dataset the Pages build serves.
/data/

# The built database. ~1.6 GB, entirely derived from data/, and rebuilt from
# scratch by build_db.py in under two minutes.
retro.sqlite

.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
